name: Fix the CSV pipeline and filter implementation
overview: Review of commit fed4969. The filter rewrite is largely correct, but the CSV download will never fire (guessed selectors), the new history exclusion destroys the only measured edge by running before the REVERSAL lane, and two measured constants were invented rather than derived.
todos:
- id: selectors content: "Replace the guessed download path in tv_scraper.py (Alt+s, button[data-name=submit], button:has-text(Export)) with the proven two-click sequence from tv_export.py: page.click('button[data-name="save-load-menu"]') then page.click('button[data-qa-id="download-btn"]'). Raise on a missing button instead of the silent 'if export_btn:' no-op" status: pending
- id: order content: "CRITICAL: move the REVERSAL BUY lane ABOVE the realvol/ret exclusions in run_data_window_filter. realvol_10d>=42.8 currently cuts 45.6% of code-20 bars, and the cut half averages +1.02% SIG while survivors are +0.07% ns. Capitulation buys are high-volatility by construction, so the exclusion removes exactly the edge it is meant to protect" status: pending
- id: constants content: "Fix the two invented constants against the corpus: P_RICH 65.0 -> 125.4 (price 2/3 quantile, 2016-2026, close>=$20) and HV_HIGH 45.0 -> 35.9 (HV20 80th pct). Add the measured value and its derivation as a comment on each" status: pending
- id: dates content: "Add date handling to csv_adapter.csv_to_datawindow: parse the 'time' column, return the snapshot bar date, reject a CSV whose last bar is older than the expected session, and decide explicitly whether to use the last (possibly forming) bar or the last confirmed one. Stamp the bar date onto the verdict" status: pending
- id: verify content: "Port tv_export.check() into the adapter: assert ncols >= MIN_COLS, nrows >= MIN_ROWS, and median bar gap <= MAX_BAR_GAP_DAYS. Without the interval check a monthly export silently makes realvol_10d a 10-MONTH volatility, which is a silent correctness failure, not a crash" status: pending
- id: fallback content: "Make the DOM fallback loud: count CSV successes vs fallbacks per run and log a warning when the CSV path fails for more than a few tickers, so a broken selector cannot masquerade as a working pipeline" status: pending
