Review of commit fed4969
What landed: src/data/csv_adapter.py (new), tests/test_csv_adapter.py (new), and edits to tv_scraper.py, data_window_filter.py, process_survivor.py.What is right
The filter rewrite is in good shape and matches the evidence:
- The dead risk/reward gate is fixed — stop = f["long_stop_loss"] at line 359, so no_room can finally fire.
- _ACTION_CODES extended to 19 SCREEN BLOCK / 20 REVERSAL BUY / 21 CHASE.
- _ACTION_ACTIONABLE_CODES correctly dropped code 5 (LOW R:R).
- The previously unmapped fields are mapped: stage_age_bars, long_in_zone, long_rr_valid, entry_at_market, ext_z_self.
- It reads the exported long_in_zone rather than recomputing the box test.
- Single PASS lane on code 20, everything else WATCH, hard exclusions ahead of both — the intended shape.
- process_survivor prefers CSV and falls back to JSON, which is the right defensive structure.
- ret_10d units are correct: the adapter returns percent and the filter compares against 12.9. Measured ignition p90 is 12.90%.


Four defects
1. The CSV download will never fire
tv_scraper.py:329:with page.expect_download(timeout=15000) as download_info:
    page.keyboard.press("Alt+s")
    export_btn = page.query_selector(
        'button[data-name="submit"], button:has-text("Export"), [data-dialog-name] button.submit-button'
    )
    if export_btn: # no else
        export_btn.click()
None of those selectors are TradingView's export control. The proven path, already in
tv_export.py lines 60-62 and 215-218, is a two-click sequence:MENU_BTN = 'button[data-name="save-load-menu"]'
DL_BTN = 'button[data-qa-id="download-btn"]'
page.click(MENU_BTN); page.click(DL_BTN)
Because if export_btn: has no else, a non-match does nothing, expect_download times out after 15s, the exception is swallowed, and the DOM fallback runs. The pipeline therefore looks implemented while realvol_10d and ret_10d are permanently None and the new exclusions never evaluate. It also costs 15 seconds per ticker.2. The history exclusion destroys the only measured edge
This is the important one. The exclusions run at lines 589-602, before the REVERSAL lane at line 604. Measured on the 6,780 code-20 bars:| Exclusion | Share of REVERSAL BUY bars cut |
|---|---|
| realvol_10d >= 42.8 | 45.6% |
| price>=65 & HV>=45 (current constants) | 13.4% |
| Ext% >= 25 | 0.0% |
| ret_10d >= 12.9 | 0.0% |
| any | 47.0% |And the half it removes is the good half:| Population | ex21 | 95% CI |
|---|---|---|
| all REVERSAL BUY | +0.85 | [+0.35, +1.38] SIG |
| survivors after exclusions | +0.07 | [-0.43, +0.57] |
| the bars cut away | +1.02 | [+0.38, +1.68] SIG |
| survivors + rev>=10 | -0.03 | [-0.56, +0.47] |The filter's one validated lane goes from +0.85 SIG to +0.07 not-significant. This is not a tuning problem: REVERSAL BUY fires on capitulation (below EMA200, RVOL>1.5, deep oversold), so elevated 10-day realised volatility is a defining property of the setup, not a warning about it.Fix: evaluate act_code == 20 before the volatility and return exclusions. The history exclusion was measured on the ignition (breakout) population and should apply there, not to the counter-trend lane.3. Two constants were invented, not measured
| Constant | In code | Measured |
|---|---|---|
| P_RICH | 65.0 | 125.4 (price 2/3 quantile, 2016-2026, close>=$20) |
| HV_HIGH | 45.0 | 35.9 (HV20 80th pct; 37.2 for 2016-2026) |The errors run in opposite directions and partly cancel — the combined clause cuts 2.4% of ignition bars with the code's values versus 3.1% with the measured ones — so this is not urgent, but both should carry their derivation in a comment so the next reader does not re-guess them.4. No date validation anywhere
csv_to_datawindow takes df.iloc[-1] with no reference to the time column at all. There is no check that the last bar is the expected session, no handling of a partially-formed intraday bar, and the bar date never reaches the verdict. For a system whose decisions are defined at bar close, a silently stale or forming last row is a correctness problem, and the old DOM path actually had more date logic than this (it picked the most recent bar not in the future).Related: nothing verifies the exported interval. tv_export.check() exists precisely because a coarser interval reaches further back and so passes a naive depth check by looking better. If an export comes back weekly or monthly, realvol_10d silently becomes a 10-week or 10-month volatility and the exclusions fire on nonsense.Minor
csv_adapter computes realised volatility from pct_change, while the 42.8 threshold was calibrated on log returns. Correlation is 0.9990 and the two disagree about crossing 42.8 on only 0.49% of bars (ignition p90: 42.79 log vs 43.29 pct), so the impact is negligible — but align one to the other.Suggested order

1. order — restore the REVERSAL lane's edge. Pure logic change, no dependencies.
2. selectors + fallback — make the CSV path actually work and fail loudly.
3. dates + verify — before trusting any live CSV.
4. constants + threshold — cheap correctness.
